          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "The change is in place. Summary of how the requirements are met:\n\n1. **Require string names** — `isinstance(name, str)` check at the very top of `Namespace.signal`, before `if name not in self`. Non-str → `TypeError(\"name must be a string\")`.\n2. **Before dictionary lookup or modification, even if the namespace already contains that key** — the check precedes the `in` lookup and the `__setitem__`, so even a `Namespace` manually seeded with a non-str key (e.g., `ns[1] = NamedSignal(1)`) will raise rather than return `ns[1]`.\n3. **Accept str subclasses and empty string** — `isinstance` accepts subclasses; `\"\"` is a `str` instance.\n4. **Module-level `signal` helper** — it is `default_namespace.signal` (a bound method), so the same validation applies; no separate code path exists.\n5. **Preserve signal identity for repeated names, original docstring, independent names, receiver dispatch** — the rest of the method body is unchanged; docstrings unchanged; no changes to `Signal`/`NamedSignal`/`NamedSignal.__init__`.\n\nAlso added a changelog entry under unreleased 1.10.0.\n\nNo local tests run (no execution tools). Submit.",
